From: Morgan Hough <morgan.hough@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 28 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] generator: cap TypeInfo::resolveType recursion depth

Qt 6.11 introduces cyclic type alias chains (most reproducibly via the
QtCore template wrappers used by QExplicitlySharedDataPointer and the
new q23::invoke_r alias). TypeInfo::resolveType has no cycle detection,
so it eventually exhausts the stack and segfaults — the crash GDB
points at:

  #0  QString::size() at qstring.h:277
  #1  comparesEqual() at qstring.h:902
  ...
  #N  TypeInfo::resolveType (recursing) codemodel.cpp:160

Cap the recursion at 64 levels (more than any real C++ type alias
chain) via a thread_local counter. On overflow, return the
partially-resolved type — the generator just emits an "unresolved"
wrapper for that one symbol instead of crashing the whole run.

This unblocks PythonQt against Qt 6.11+ system headers on Fedora.

--- a/generator/parser/codemodel.cpp
+++ b/generator/parser/codemodel.cpp
@@ -141,6 +141,16 @@ TypeInfo TypeInfo::combine(const TypeInfo& __lhs, const TypeInfo& __rhs)

 TypeInfo TypeInfo::resolveType(TypeInfo const& __type, CodeModelItem __scope)
 {
+  // Qt 6.11 introduces cyclic type alias chains that send this recursion
+  // off forever (eventually exhausting the stack and segfaulting). Cap
+  // the depth via a thread-local counter and degrade gracefully on
+  // overflow: returning the partially-resolved type just means the
+  // generator emits an "unresolved" wrapper for that one symbol.
+  static thread_local int __depth = 0;
+  if (__depth >= 64) {
+    return __type;
+  }
+
   CodeModel* __model = __scope->model();
   Q_ASSERT(__model != 0);

@@ -156,8 +166,12 @@ TypeInfo TypeInfo::resolveType(TypeInfo const& __type, CodeModelItem __scope)
     otherType.setQualifiedName(__item->qualifiedName());
   }

-  if (TypeAliasModelItem __alias = __item.dynamicCast<_TypeAliasModelItem>())
-    return resolveType(TypeInfo::combine(__alias->type(), otherType), __scope);
+  if (TypeAliasModelItem __alias = __item.dynamicCast<_TypeAliasModelItem>()) {
+    ++__depth;
+    TypeInfo __result = resolveType(TypeInfo::combine(__alias->type(), otherType), __scope);
+    --__depth;
+    return __result;
+  }

   return otherType;
 }
